    "updated_at": "2017-01-14T11:14:49Z",
    "body": "I guess an iframe would need to be used to control the size of the viewport. Then these cases seem interesting:\r\n\r\n* viewport tall\r\n* viewport wide\r\n* viewport square\r\n* dialog smaller than viewport in block flow direction\r\n* dialog same size as viewport in block flow direction\r\n* dialog bigger than viewport in block flow direction\r\n* viewport horizontal writing mode\r\n* viewport vertical writing mode\r\n* viewport horizontal, dialog's parent and dialog itself vertical\r\n* viewport vertical, dialog's parent and dialog itself horizontal \r\n\r\nI think it's not necessary to test all possible writing-mode/direction combinations, as that is probably tested separately.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
